<title>USA: ThermoTrex buys Computer Communications.</title>
<headline>ThermoTrex buys Computer Communications.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>ThermoTrex Corp has acquired Computer Communications Specialists Inc for about $10 million, subject to a post-closing adjustment.</p>
<p>Founded in 1977, CCS specializes in developing and marketing interactive voice-response systems, which enable callers to access a wide variety of information by pressing buttons on a touch-tone phone.</p>
<p>Atlanta-based CCS had revenues of about $15 million in 1996.</p>
</text>
